cpp-stage3.jsonl and go-stage3.jsonl describe two workspaces of the public
repository bazelbuild/examples (https://github.com/bazelbuild/examples), rev
efab5bd4660ebfe720bd52efaeeccefaf00ee4ad: cpp-tutorial/stage3 and
go-tutorial/stage3. That repository is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0); glia's own licence
is separate and does not apply to it.

They are `bazel query '//...:*' --output=streamed_jsonproto` output in the
shape of bazel's build.proto `Target` message printed by protobuf's JsonFormat
(src/main/protobuf/build.proto and query2/query/output/
StreamedJSONProtoOutputFormatter.java at bazel 7.4.0, the version
go-tutorial/stage3/.bazelversion pins), one target per line. They were written
by hand from the two workspaces' BUILD files: no bazel could be run when they
were made (glia 0.5.7, packet HT.3), so the targets, labels, attributes and
locations follow those BUILD files and build.proto, and the attribute sets of
each rule class are an approximation of what bazel prints. Absolute paths read
`/WORKSPACE/..`, the workspace root, which the tests replace with a temporary
directory.
